# =============================================================================
# .github/CODEOWNERS
# =============================================================================
# VG-12'S HUMAN-APPROVAL HALF, WHICH IS A POLICY AND NOT A JOB.
#
# STRATEGY section 4.2 gives VG-12 four parts: `--frozen-lockfile`, SCA, SBOM,
# and "human approval for any new package". CI-05 enforces the first three
# mechanically. The fourth cannot be a workflow step, because a job can see that
# the dependency surface changed and cannot see that a human agreed to it.
# Pretending otherwise would produce the worst available outcome: a green check
# that reads as an approval nobody gave.
#
# So the approval is enforced where GitHub can enforce it, by making a change to
# any of the files below require this repository's owner as a reviewer. THE
# BRANCH PROTECTION RULE IS THE OTHER HALF OF THIS FILE and it is not in the
# repository: "Require review from Code Owners" must be on for the default
# branch, or this file is documentation. CI-05 prints the dependency surface it
# sees change on a pull request, so the requirement is visible in the log
# whether or not the setting is on.
#
# WHY THE LIST IS THE FILES AND NOT `package.json` ALONE. A package enters this
# tree through four doors: a manifest, the catalog that resolves its version,
# the lockfile that pins its tree, and the `.npmrc` settings that decide whether
# any of that is enforced. `save-exact` turned off is a new package admission
# with no diff on any manifest.

# The dependency surface, VG-12.
/pnpm-workspace.yaml    @lam2-coder
/pnpm-lock.yaml         @lam2-coder
/.npmrc                 @lam2-coder
/package.json           @lam2-coder
apps/*/package.json     @lam2-coder
packages/*/package.json @lam2-coder

# The gates themselves. A workflow edit can turn any gate in this repository off
# and the diff that does it is three characters.
/.github/workflows/     @lam2-coder
/.github/CODEOWNERS     @lam2-coder
/scripts/               @lam2-coder
/packages/tooling/      @lam2-coder
/packages/eslint-plugin-merit/ @lam2-coder
/.semgrep/              @lam2-coder

# Migrations are sacred: forward-only, reviewed on main, never edited after
# merge, only superseded, and every money-path file gets the founder's
# line-by-line read (constitution E2). This line does not create that
# requirement, it makes GitHub ask for it.
/packages/db/migrations/ @lam2-coder
